<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 88.3 percent of their 1996/97 maize crop by May 30, the Agriculture Secretariat said in weekly crop report Friday.</p>
<p>This compared with only 81.2 percent progress by the same date the previous season. Soybean harvesting was 95.4 percent complete, compared with 84.5 percent progress by the same date in 1996. Cotton harvesting was 71.6 percent complete, compared with 60.6 percent progress at the same stage last season. Good rains fell throughout most grains areas. Rain varied, with precipitation concentrated in Buenos Aires and La Pampa provinces in addition to the north of the country.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Maize     3,926  100.0(100.0) 2,887.8   88.3  (81.2)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,072.7   95.4  (84.5)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0  (100.0</p>
<p> Sorghum     784  100.0(100.0)   656.9   92.0  (82.2)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   632.7   71.6  (60.6)</p>
<p>((--Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
